---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import ShortcutReference from '../../components/ShortcutReference.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="Developer Keyboard Shortcut Reference" description="Quick reference for common VS Code, Chrome DevTools, and terminal keyboard shortcuts.">
  <ShortcutReference client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why a few shortcuts save real time daily</h2>
  <p>Small, frequent actions (opening a file, searching command history, toggling a comment) get performed dozens of times a day — the seconds saved per action from keyboard shortcuts compound into meaningfully faster workflow over a full working day.</p>

  <h2>How to use this reference</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Pick the tool category (VS Code, Chrome DevTools, Terminal).</li>
    <li>Learn a few shortcuts at a time rather than trying to memorize everything at once.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Trying to memorize every shortcut at once</strong> instead of gradually incorporating a few frequently-used ones into muscle memory.</li>
    <li><strong>Not checking for platform differences</strong> — many shortcuts differ between Windows/Linux (Ctrl) and Mac (Cmd) keybindings.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Use cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Learning essential shortcuts for a newly adopted tool</li>
    <li>Quickly looking up a specific shortcut you've forgotten</li>
    <li>Onboarding a new team member to commonly used development tool shortcuts</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <p><strong>Do these shortcuts work the same on Mac and Windows?</strong> The listed shortcuts note both Ctrl (Windows/Linux) and Cmd (Mac) variants where they differ — check the specific tool's own documentation for any additional platform-specific differences.</p>
</ToolLayout>
